# {{ project }}

A Phalcon MVC application.

## Run it

With docker:

    ./crest up
    ./crest install

With rootless docker, set `UID=0` and `GID=0` in `.env` first.

With PHP and composer on the host:

    composer install
    crest serve

Then open http://localhost:{{ port }}/.

## Layout

| Path | Contents |
|---|---|
| `{{ documentRoot }}/index.php` | The web entry point |
| `{{ source }}/{{ front }}.php` | The front controller: container, providers, application. Add a provider in `providers()` |
| `{{ providerPath }}/` | The providers of the services |
| `{{ controllerPath }}/` | The controllers. `GET /` is `{{ controllerPath }}/{{ seed }}.php` |
| `{{ controllerPath }}/{{ baseFolder }}/` | The base of the controllers. crest writes it; do not edit it |
| `{{ viewsPath }}/` | The views. `GET /` shows the view `index/index` in the layout `index` |
| `crest.php` | The crest configuration |

## Next steps

These commands use the crest in `vendor/`, with the autoloader and the
Phalcon of this project. On the host, a global crest passes them to it. With
the docker runtime in `crest.php` (the default of `crest new`), it runs them
in the `{{ service }}` container:

    crest make:controller Users

Without a global crest, use `./crest`. It needs docker only, and it runs them
in the `{{ service }}` container:

    ./crest make:controller Users
